  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff in July 2023. The project has expanded its team with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray and secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with the next phase focusing on UI enhancements starting in October. The budget has been adjusted to $550,000, with an additional $55,000 allocated for compliance training and audits. The project is moving from the design phase to development under the guidance of lead developer Omar Jensen. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated for implementation next January."
